# Universal AI Coding Agent Instructions & Engineering Standards

1. 90% Unit Test Code Coverage Benchmark (Strict Per-File Enforcement)
- Maintain >= 90% coverage on Statements, Branches, Functions, and Lines on every file in frontend/ and backend/.
- Verify via `npm run test:coverage` and `npm run check:coverage`.

2. Global Test Timeout: 20,000 ms.

3. User Prompt History Maintenance (`prompts.md`)
- Maintain `prompts.md` in workspace root.
- Store ONLY user-provided prompts with timestamps and prompt text. Do NOT record AI-generated output.

4. Structured Centralized Logging & Logs Storage
- Store persistent logs in `backend/logs/` (`app.log`, `error.log`, `audit.log`) with auto-purging and searchability.
- Apply detailed structured logging across all backend and frontend layers.

5. Database Optimization & Query Efficiency Standard
- Audit database queries for optimal execution paths, avoiding full table scans and redundant roundtrips.
- Implement intelligent query caching with TTL and automatic write-through invalidation to minimize cloud database compute hours.
- Tune connection pool lifecycle to reclaim idle connections and minimize compute usage.

6. GraphQL Integration & Streamlined Fetching
- Provide a unified `/graphql` endpoint for fine-grained field selection and batched data retrieval across enterprise entities.

7. Tech Stack LTS/Stable Version Upgrade & Dependency Maintenance Protocol
- Regularly audit, upgrade, and maintain all core tech stack components, runtime environments, framework dependencies, and libraries to latest LTS/stable releases.
- Systematically refactor breaking changes and deprecations, validating via full test suite, linting, typechecks, and 90% per-file coverage.

8. Auto-Resolve Bugs & Errors in Logs Standard
- Continuously parse and diagnose runtime log outputs, stack traces, and error codes from `backend/logs/` and runtime streams to apply automated root-cause fixes.
- Verify all fixes against the full quality pipeline with zero regressions.

9. Auto-Resolve Warnings Standard
- Proactively detect and resolve all compiler, linter, runtime, React hook, and dependency warnings across frontend and backend.
- Apply safe refactoring for deprecation notices, unused imports, type mismatches, and non-standard syntax.

10. Automated Performance Optimization Standard
- Continuously audit and optimize critical execution paths, API payloads, query latencies, code-splitting, lazy-loading, and multi-tier resource caching.

11. Quality Check Pipeline & Multi-Project Verification Protocol
- Run `npm run check:quality` (`npm run qc`) after changes to verify:
  1. Build (`npm run build`)
  2. Unit test coverage (`npm run test:coverage` & `npm run check:coverage`)
  3. Typecheck (`npm run typecheck`)
  4. Lint (`npm run lint`)
  5. DB migrations (`npm run db:migrate`)
- Run `npm run check:fast` (`npm run qc:fast`) for fast change validation.

12. CI/CD Workflow & PR Summary Comment Standard
- Enforce full quality check pipeline on PRs via `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
- Automatically generate and post PR comments with unit test pass/fail counts and per-file coverage metrics.

13. Environment Variables Example Maintenance & Secrets Sanitation Standard
- Keep `.env.example`, `backend/.env.example`, and `frontend/.env.example` updated with all required configuration variables.
- Never hardcode sensitive secrets in source code; read from `process.env` with fallback defaults.

14. Comprehensive and Descriptive UI Error Messaging Standard
- Implement user-facing error messages that clearly present actionable context, specific failure details, and remediation guidance across Form Validation, Network, Database/Sync, Authentication, and Business Logic categories.

15. Strict Input Schema Validation Standard
- Define all validation schemas in dedicated constants modules (`backend/src/config/validationSchemas.js` and `frontend/lib/validationSchemas.ts`).
- Validate all incoming user and system inputs (forms, API routes, controller bodies, query params, headers) against schema constants before processing.

16. Dedicated Separate Constants Standard
- Store all constants, configurations, and UI strings in separate dedicated files (`backend/src/config/constants.js`, `frontend/lib/constants.ts`, `frontend/lib/uiStrings.ts`).

17. Dedicated Separate Types & Interfaces Standard
- Keep all TypeScript interfaces and data models centralized in `frontend/lib/types.ts` and `backend/src/config/types.js`. Use `import type`.

18. Strictest Linter & Code Quality Standard
- Enforce strict typing (`no-explicit-any`, `no-non-null-assertion`, `consistent-type-imports`, `prefer-optional-chain`), accessibility (`jsx-a11y`), React hooks, and ES6+ style conventions in CI/CD and build gates.
